---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';
const meta = {
  title: `Privacy policy — ${SITE.name}`,
  description: 'What data this site collects, why, and your choices.',
  path: '/privacy-policy/',
};
---
<BaseLayout meta={meta}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--color-muted)">
      This is a privacy-conscious starter policy, not legal advice. It must be reviewed against
      the laws that apply to your audience and the tools you actually run before launch. See
      docs/GTM_GA4_SETUP.md and Section 9 of the build brief.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is a static website. We don't ask you to create an account and we don't
      collect names, emails, or payment details through the site itself.
    </p>
    <p>
      If analytics is enabled, we use Google Analytics 4 (loaded through Google Tag Manager) to
      understand, in aggregate, which articles are read and which links are clicked. This uses
      cookies or similar identifiers. We configure it to avoid collecting personal information
      such as emails, names, or phone numbers, and affiliate-click tracking records only the
      link, its position, and the product — never anything about you personally.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      When you click an Amazon link and visit Amazon, Amazon's own privacy policy and cookies
      apply. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can block cookies and analytics in your browser; the site remains fully functional
      with analytics blocked. If your audience is in a region that requires consent before
      analytics runs (for example the EU/UK), a consent banner is required — this starter does
      not ship one. See the setup docs for how to add a consent management platform to GTM.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
